eaststroke legs, he was chased on the final leg by Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/134800"} "Daiya Seto"] ", who had the second fastest freestyle split (after " [:a {:href "/athletes/145834"} "Lewis Clareburt"] " (NZL), who finished seventh). But Seto was too far behind on the final turn and Marchand held him off by 0.28 seconds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Marchand became the only athlete at Paris 2024 to win four gold medals, in any sport, and he added a fifth with his bronze in the men’s medley relay. He joined Americans " [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/51572"} "Mark Spitz"] ", and East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/47512"} "Kristin Otto"] " as the only swimmers to win four individual gold medals at a single edition of the Olympic Games. Phelps won four in 2004 and five in 2008, Spitz won four in 1972, and Otto won her four in 1988."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/142925"} "Léon Marchand"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "1:57.86 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "1:56.31 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:54.06 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134067"} "Duncan Scott"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "1:57.77 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "1:56.49 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:55.31 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122353"} "Wang Shun"]]